<title>SWEDEN: FIRMER SWEDISH DEBT SOFTENS ON EMU UNCERTAINTY.</title>
<headline>FIRMER SWEDISH DEBT SOFTENS ON EMU UNCERTAINTY.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish debt yields fell across the board on Friday pushed by the stronger U.S. market. Lower German yields also lent support, dealers said.</p>
<p>EMU uncertainity, however, continued to put a damper on the Swedish market and morning gains soon reversed a little.</p>
<p>Six-month T-bill rates dropped one basis point to 4.53 percent and the nine-year bond yield was three basis points lower at 7.30 percent compared to 7.28 percent earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;The underlying reason for us doing less well than in the rest of Europe is the fact we trade on convergency and not on fundamentals,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
</text>
